  '{"blocks":[{"type":"voiceover","audio_files":["grant-chiasson/qb-program/lesson_01/seg_01.mp3"],"total_audio_seconds":87.28,"timed_text":[{"start_s":0.0,"text":"May 15, you chose your focus anchor earlier in this program, a word or"},{"start_s":5.84,"text":"Phrase your mind returns to when it starts to drift."},{"start_s":9.34,"text":"Today I want to take that further because the most powerful version of an"},{"start_s":14.28,"text":"Anchor isn''t just a word in your head, it''s something physical, something"},{"start_s":18.72,"text":"That exists in the actual space where you compete."},{"start_s":22.7,"text":"Elite athletes do this instinctively, a basketball player who bounces the"},{"start_s":27.16,"text":"Ball exactly three times before a free throw, a sprinter who locks eyes on"},{"start_s":31.74,"text":"The same spot on the track before the gun, a quarterback who taps his wrist"},{"start_s":36.02,"text":"Band before walking to the line, these aren''t superstitions, they''re"},{"start_s":40.42,"text":"Trained focus triggers, physical anchors that pull the mind back to the"},{"start_s":45.42,"text":"Present moment on command."},{"start_s":47.86,"text":"The key is consistency, the same thing the same way every single time,"},{"start_s":54.06,"text":"Because your nervous system responds to patterns."},{"start_s":57.26,"text":"When you perform that cue enough times in a focused state, the cue begins"},{"start_s":62.06,"text":"To trigger the state, that is conditioning,"},{"start_s":66.68,"text":"That''s what we''re building today."},{"start_s":69.08,"text":"Think about the physical environment where you compete."},{"start_s":72.46,"text":"What is something you can see, touch, feel or do?"},{"start_s":77.12,"text":"Something that is always available in that space that you can turn into"},{"start_s":81.28,"text":"Your competition anchor."},{"start_s":83.52,"text":"On your screen, you''re going to identify it and lock it in."}]},{"type":"flash_cards","cards":[{"front":"Flash Card 1: \"Think about the physical space where you compete. What do you see, hear, or feel in that environment that is always there — every competition, every time?\"","back":"Text Entry 1: Athlete describes their competition environment. Saved to journal."},{"front":"Flash Card 2: \"Identify your physical anchor — something in that space, or something you wear or carry, that you can use as a consistent focus trigger. Something you can touch, see, or do deliberately before or during competition.\"","back":"Text Entry 2: Athlete names and describes their physical anchor. Saved to profile."}],"ambient_audio":"ambient/ambient_music.mp3"},{"type":"voiceover","audio_files":["grant-chiasson/qb-program/lesson_01/seg_02.mp3"],"total_audio_seconds":20.14,"timed_text":[{"start_s":0.0,"text":"Every time you use the physical anchor, you''re strengthening the connection"},{"start_s":3.64,"text":"Between that action and your focus state."},{"start_s":6.62,"text":"Do it in practice, do it in warmups, do it in competition."},{"start_s":11.12,"text":"The more consistent you are, the faster it works when the pressure is real."},{"start_s":16.26,"text":"Check out the journal and have to finish."},{"start_s":17.96,"text":"Day 15 is complete."}]},{"type":"journal_prompt","prompt":"What physical anchor did you choose — and why does that specific thing feel right for your competition environment?"}]}'::jsonb
